## Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this SvelteKit project.

### Changes Made

**1. Installed Package**
- Added `@vercel/analytics` v2.0.1 as a dependency
- Used `--legacy-peer-deps` flag to handle peer dependency conflict with SvelteKit v3

**2. Modified Files**
- `src/routes/+layout.ts` - Added analytics initialization code
  - Imported `dev` from `$app/environment`
  - Imported `injectAnalytics` from `@vercel/analytics/sveltekit`
  - Called `injectAnalytics()` with automatic mode detection (development vs production)
  - Preserved existing `prerender = true` export

**3. Updated Dependencies**
- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics to dependencies
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new package and its dependencies

### Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), the analytics are initialized in the root layout file (`+layout.ts`) which ensures tracking is active across all pages.

The implementation:
- Automatically detects development vs production mode using SvelteKit's `$app/environment`
- Integrates seamlessly with the existing prerendered static site configuration
- Adds no visible UI changes - analytics run silently in the background

### Verification

✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
✅ All existing functionality preserved
✅ Lock file updated properly

### Next Steps

To enable analytics:
1. Deploy this code to Vercel
2. Navigate to your project's Analytics section in the Vercel dashboard
3. Click "Enable" to start collecting analytics data

Analytics will automatically begin tracking page views and visitor data once enabled in the dashboard.
